<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">companion-ask</ansi>

Sends your companion to ask someone here about something for you. Only
when you send them this way do your companion's words reach that person's
dialogue, and only on that topic, for a short while.

You must be able to see who you are sending them to. Another player's
companion cannot be asked.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">companion-ask <who> about <what></ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">companion-ask smith about the ore</ansi>
  This sends your companion to put that question to the smith.

The person is named by one word, as with other commands. Everything after
the word <ansi fg="command">about</ansi> is the topic.

See also <ansi fg="command">help aicompanion</ansi>.
